WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.793
There's no need to roll the dice on understanding
the end of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor Among Thieves."

00:00:05.793 --> 00:00:08.966
Here's how that ending came together — no
DM required.

00:00:08.966 --> 00:00:11.769
Game on
With the resurgence of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons,"

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:16.000
it's only fitting that Paramount set out to
bring it to the big screen once again with

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.369
"Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor Among Thieves."

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:23.681
The adventure takes place in the legendary
Forgotten Realms campaign setting of the tabletop game.

00:00:23.681 --> 00:00:29.769
It focuses on two original characters: Edgin
and Holga, two thieves who embark on an adventure

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:31.310
to right a past wrong.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:36.860
The pair's last heist ended up putting a powerful
artifact in the hands of a Red Wizard named

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:41.289
Sofina, and by the time we catch up with them,
they're on a mission to take it back.

00:00:41.289 --> 00:00:46.050
Unfortunately, their former ally Forge is
now working with Sofina and has turned Edgin's

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.030
daughter Kira against them.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:53.480
Now, Edgin and Holga must form a new team
to retrieve the artifact and stop Forge and

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.480
Sofina's nefarious plans.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:00.390
Like any great "Dungeons &amp; Dragons" quest,
these unlikely heroes face many dangers and

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.050
shocking surprises during their campaign.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:07.440
The film's finale has the most shocking moments
of all, though, as the group comes face to

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.760
face with Forge and Sofina to fight for the
people of Neverwinter.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:15.460
So, let's delve into the ending of "Honor
Among Thieves" and the biggest moments of

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.151
its action-packed climax.

00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:19.855
"This is unlike anything we've ever seen."

00:01:19.855 --> 00:01:23.720
Although Forge and Sofina have been working
together for quite some time, they aren't

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.740
quite on the same page.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.049
Sofina would rather kill Forge than continue
to work with him and Forge only has his mind

00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:32.370
set on maintaining his wealth and power.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:36.290
These separate motivations see them part ways
in the film's finale.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.150
Forge plans on abandoning Neverwinter and
stealing the riches of those he's invited

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.150
to the games.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:46.390
He plans to sail towards a new horizon while
Sofina turns everyone into mindless servants.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:50.060
Sofina, on the other hand, isn't leaving the
stadium at all.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.899
Instead, she's going to fulfill her destiny
as a Red Wizard to become all-powerful and

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:56.329
rule over the lands.

00:01:56.329 --> 00:02:01.390
With the help of the magical horn she enlisted
Edgin and his group to steal years prior,

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.210
Sofina is set to turn the people of Neverwinter
into her undead army by unleashing a powerful

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.189
mist that will kill and reanimate anyone caught
in its path.

00:02:10.189 --> 00:02:14.620
Forge has set her up for success by bringing
everyone into a packed arena to be put under

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:15.620
her spell.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.890
At first, it seems like their plan is going
to come together flawlessly, but they don't

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.740
count on Edgin and his team spoiling their
fun.

00:02:23.048 --> 00:02:28.430
A key part of Edgin's original plan is having
the group's sorcerer Simon attune to a magical

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.709
helmet that will nullify the spell protecting
Forge's vault.

00:02:31.709 --> 00:02:33.264
"Protect it with your very life."

00:02:33.264 --> 00:02:34.323
"I will."

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:36.830
"Hold this."

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:41.650
However, Simon's lack of confidence keeps
him from being able to use the helmet properly.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.349
Every time Simon puts the helmet on, he's
transported to another world where he meets

00:02:45.349 --> 00:02:47.239
his extremely judgy ancestor.

00:02:47.239 --> 00:02:52.159
He tries to attune with the helmet multiple
times but gets frustrated and tells Edgin

00:02:52.159 --> 00:02:53.330
that he can't do it.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.739
Although the group is forced to go with another
plan, Edgin never gives up on Simon.

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:02.820
In a crucial moment, Edgin tells Simon that
he's better than he gives himself credit for.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:07.129
Any time that the group has desperately needed
Simon and his skills he has always managed

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:08.209
to deliver.

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:11.510
This pep talk turns out to be exactly what
Simon needs.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:16.115
When Simon gets in front of the vault door,
he tries to attune with the helmet one last time.

00:03:16.115 --> 00:03:21.190
With this newfound confidence, Simon fights
past his ancestor's doubts and even punches

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:24.739
him in the face to earn his respect and show
his spirit.

00:03:24.739 --> 00:03:29.379
This allows Simon to finally attune to the
helmet, open the door, and become even better

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:30.379
at magic.

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:35.049
Edgin might be the group's self-proclaimed
planner, but he isn't exactly the best at

00:03:35.049 --> 00:03:36.049
his chosen role.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.851
"If the existing plan fails, I make a new
plan."

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.707
"So you make plans that fail?"

00:03:39.707 --> 00:03:40.207
"No."

00:03:40.207 --> 00:03:41.207
"He also plays the lute."

00:03:41.477 --> 00:03:42.162
"No relevant."

00:03:42.162 --> 00:03:47.596
While his determination is admirable, everything
around him and his companions can fall apart quickly.

00:03:47.596 --> 00:03:52.910
As the group heads into the big heist sequence,
Edgin is constantly changing and altering

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.480
the plan to cover up obstacles and failures.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:02.019
His Plan A becomes a Plan C and his Plan B
becomes a Plan D. Ultimately, he ends up combining

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:07.920
both strategies to form one super heist plan
that somehow works, although not without some

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.620
unexpected chaos.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:13.469
Maybe Edgin deserves more credit and has a
better grip on the situation than it seems

00:04:13.469 --> 00:04:16.700
-- or maybe he's just winging it and rolling
twenties.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:21.120
Either way, Edgin's planning is often bizarre
and frequently puts the mission in jeopardy

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.196
-- especially in the final mission.

00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:28.259
When the time comes for the group to take
their shot at stopping Forge and Sofina, things

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:31.020
end up being much more chaotic than expected.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:35.800
The group is forced to pivot towards a new
plan after Simon can't attune with the helmet,

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.600
but this approach shows surprising promise.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.539
The group uses the Hither and Thither Staff
to set up a portal in a painting stashed on

00:04:43.539 --> 00:04:48.380
a wagon delivering valuable items to Forge
as a way to gain access to the vault.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.450
Unfortunately, the painting falls over when
the guards put it in the vault, which means

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.770
the only thing the group can see is the concrete
floor.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:00.710
With that plan suddenly thwarted, Edgin decides
to jump back to the original idea of having

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.600
Simon attune with the helmet.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:07.100
However, Doric realizes that she might be
able to create a hole small enough for her

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.930
to transform into a worm to slither through.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:16.727
Edgin decides that both plans will run concurrently,
and this seeming chaos results in some shocking success.

00:05:16.727 --> 00:05:21.169
Doric is able to chip a hole big enough that
she can get through as a worm and is even

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:24.150
able to cover up the portal before the guards
can see it.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:28.930
Even better, Simon is able to attune the helmet
and break the magic seal keeping the vault

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:29.930
door protected.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:35.360
Although both of Edgin's plans work and everyone
-- except for him -- makes it into the vault,

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.570
they encounter an unexpected problem.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:43.220
The door that Simon opens leads him and Holga
to an empty room while Doric is quickly knocked

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:47.639
out after she sees Forge's men loading the
valuables on an escape boat.

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:52.410
While this is all happening, Edgin is giving
a tearful apology to Kira, promising to be

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.930
a better father to her.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:59.330
Unfortunately, Kira is actually Sofina in
disguise and Edgin is suddenly tied up by

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.520
tentacles, as are Holga and Simon.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.100
Desperate to evade death, Edgin suggests that
Sofina and Forge put him and his group into

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:11.940
the games that Forge is hosting so that they
have a chance to earn their lives.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:15.550
Forge isn't willing to approve his request,
but Sofina is.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:19.660
She knows that even if they survive the games,
they'll simply become zombies for the army

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:23.040
of undead when she spreads the deadly mist
throughout the arena.

00:06:23.187 --> 00:06:29.593
"There will be a wonderful gift for each and
every one of you."

00:06:29.593 --> 00:06:34.130
Edgin might've helped the group escape a quick
death at the hands of Sofina, but no one is

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:36.150
happy about where they are now.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:40.520
Both Doric and Simon are unable to use their
magical abilities as they are cuffed with

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.720
a relic that negates their magic.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.000
Beyond that, their first task in the tournament
has death written all over it.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:51.639
The first round of the games has contestants
traverse a maze before being slaughtered by

00:06:51.639 --> 00:06:53.620
a vicious displacer beast.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.009
The maze itself has plenty of obstacles that
could kill players -- including walls that

00:06:58.009 --> 00:07:02.900
fall to expose their position, mimics that
trick warriors looking for weapons, and a

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.520
gelatinous cube that digests organisms that
fall into it.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:11.180
However, the gelatinous cube actually comes
in handy for Doric as she uses it to remove

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.630
her magic-restraining cuffs and help the group
escape.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:19.011
Doric's quick thinking might mean that Edgin
has a new rival for being the group's planner.

00:07:19.498 --> 00:07:23.960
Before embarking on the quest to retrieve
the helmet, Edgin promises Xenk that he will

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.540
give the riches stolen by Forge to the poorest
citizens of Neverwinter.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:33.380
Given that the group is full of thieves, it
initially feels unlikely that Edgin will keep

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:34.660
his promise.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.150
As it turns out, he does.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:41.099
In a fitting bit of payback against Forge,
the group sends his valuables tumbling across

00:07:41.099 --> 00:07:43.620
the city thanks to the Hither and Thither
Staff.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:49.240
While the revenge is satisfying, the lure
of gold also helps evacuate the arena, allowing

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.210
the group to spoil Sofina's plan.

00:07:51.644 --> 00:07:56.639
With her plan thwarted by Edgin's group, Sofina
is furious and ready to take the party on

00:07:56.639 --> 00:08:01.110
herself, leading to an epic, all-out brawl
in the middle of town.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:06.205
Doric transforms into an owlbear for some
destructive combat, but is eventually knocked out.

00:08:06.205 --> 00:08:10.639
Holga and Edgin hold their own for a bit,
but are eventually sent spinning through the

00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:13.509
town inside a bubble Sofina traps them in.

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:18.319
Simon stands the best chance against Sofina,
but the villain still comes out on top.

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:22.860
Once Sofina has them all in her grasp, she
attempts to use a time-stop spell to make

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.710
it easier for her to kill them.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:29.919
However, when Edgin starts moving it's revealed
that Simon was able to stop the spell.

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:35.120
It's a great moment for Simon that's made
better when an invisible Kira places the magic-negation

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.200
cuff on Sofina to restrain her powers.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:42.990
Doric then wastes no time turning back into
an owlbear and hilariously throws Sofina around

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:46.279
like a rag doll until she's crushed by some
falling debris.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:51.750
With Sofina finally dead and Neverwinter saved,
it seems like the group's journey has ended.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:56.310
However, their cheers of victory are interrupted
when they see that Holga has been stabbed

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.430
by one of Sofina's daggers.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:02.899
Since the dagger is imbued with Red Wizard
magic, Simon's powers won't be able to save

00:09:02.899 --> 00:09:05.230
Holga -- she's going to die.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:09.570
Although she knows she's doomed, Holga is
proud that she was slain in battle and fulfilled

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:13.600
the mission of her people by protecting the
helmet while stopping a Red Wizard.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.357
Plus, she feels like her family is right by
her side and is happy she did enough to protect them.

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:24.490
Edgin and Kira help Holga pass on by singing
one of Edgin's old melodies until the infection

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:27.600
caused by the Red Wizard's magic consumes
her.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:32.290
It's a tragic end for Holga, especially since
she's become a mother figure for the group

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.290
and Kira.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:38.210
When he sees how devastated Kira is, Edgin
makes a difficult choice.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:42.060
After spending the film desperately wanting
to use the Tablet of Reawakening to resurrect

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.649
his wife, he has a change of heart when he
sees how much Holga means to Kira.

00:09:46.649 --> 00:09:50.250
Ultimately, he decides to use the tablet to
bring Holga back.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:54.709
It's an immensely fulfilling moment in Edgin's
character arc and a big step in his journey

00:09:54.709 --> 00:09:57.080
to become a better father and a better person.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.730
Sure, it's a crushing blow for Edgin since
it ensures that he will never see his wife

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:05.314
again, but in his heart he knows that it's
what's best for his daughter.

00:10:05.516 --> 00:10:10.750
With Sofina defeated and their group reunited,
the four adventurers take refuge at the Wood

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.920
Elf enclave and talk about their time together.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.320
Edgin and Holga discuss what they might do
next, and Simon takes a shot at asking Doric

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.320
out again.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.899
This time, she takes him up on the offer,
and Simon seems delighted.

00:10:22.899 --> 00:10:27.540
Forge attempts to escape through the woods
but is stopped by Xenk and taken to prison.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:32.240
There, we see him attempt to plead his case
for parole -- just as Edgin and Holga did

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.769
at the beginning of the movie.

00:10:33.769 --> 00:10:36.180
However, he is far less successful.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:40.570
By the end of the film, it doesn't seem like
Edgin and the group need to worry about Forge

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:45.000
any time soon and can continue on in peace
-- for now, at least.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.190
Now for the biggest question of them all -- is
"Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor Among Thieves"

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.000
going to have a sequel?

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.180
At the moment, there has been no word of a
follow-up film and the movie's mid-credit

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.540
scene doesn't give any answers.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:03.899
It's mostly just a last laugh to send moviegoers
out on, but the signs of a sequel happening

00:11:03.899 --> 00:11:05.190
are very good.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:09.740
The reactions and reviews for "Dungeons &amp; Dragons:
Honor Among Thieves" have been incredibly

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:14.660
positive so far and the movie has the potential
to be a solid hit at the box office.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:19.310
If "Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor Among Thieves"
is a big success, don't be surprised to hear

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:22.760
that Edgin and his crew are returning for
another adventure.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:27.959
We do know that Sofina had a superior Red
Wizard who could easily make for an antagonist

00:11:27.959 --> 00:11:29.490
in a follow-up movie.

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:34.350
On the other hand, "Dungeons &amp; Dragons" has
the potential to be a bigger franchise, touching

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:38.470
on stories outside of the one presented in
"Honor Among Thieves."

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:42.930
With how expansive the "Dungeons &amp; Dragons"
property is, thanks to its different campaigns

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:47.940
and settings, this franchise could easily
have plenty of spinoffs that introduce radically

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.709
different characters, stories, and genres.

00:11:50.709 --> 00:11:55.460
If this first movie does well enough, we could
be seeing a lot more "Dungeons &amp; Dragons"

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.848
content in theaters for years to come.

00:11:57.848 --> 00:12:00.239
"Anything you want to add?"

00:12:00.596 --> 00:12:01.556
"I'm good."

